ymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTimeSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The time-symbol type indicates how to display a time signature. The normal value is the usual fractional"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"display, and is the implied symbol type if none is specified. Other options are the common and cut time"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, as well as a single number with an implied denominator. The note symbol indicates that the beat-type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should be represented with the corresponding downstem note rather than a number. The dotted-note symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicates that the beat-type should be represented with a dotted downstem note that corresponds to three times","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the beat-type value, and a numerator that is one third the beats value.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTimeSymbol"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTime":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Time signatures are represented by the beats element for the numerator and the beat-type element for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"denominator. The symbol attribute is used to indicate common and cut time symbols as well as a single number"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"display. Multiple pairs of beat and beat-type elements are used for composite time signatures with multiple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"denominators, such as 2\/4 + 3\/8. A composite such as 3+2\/8 requires only one beat\/beat-type pair.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLTime","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTime","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTime","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltime","identifi